# O Christmas Tree, arranged by Claude and SZ. A soft string chord, then woodwinds over a gentle waltz bass.
title: O Christmas Tree
composer: Traditional (German)
arranger: Claude & SZ
about: The German O Tannenbaum. Ernst Anschütz wrote the best-known words in 1824 from an older folk song praising the fir tree for staying green all winter. Only later did it become a Christmas song.
year: traditional
source: public-domain
category: carols
key: G major
style: orchestral
tempo: 92
time: 3/4

@bars 48-51 tempo=92..70

